  "description": "<p>This ticket is document the information stored in a resource that is exposed as headers but does need to be persisted in the import-export process.</p>\n\n<p>An examples is the version information via the /fcr:versions Link header.</p>\n\n<p>This could be documented here, or in some other import-export design page.</p>\n\n<p>List of Headers:</p>\n\n<p><b>All resources:</b> </p>\n\n<p>Content-Type:  what are we doing now? Relying on the extension of the exported file?</p>\n\n<p><b>For mementos</b></p>\n\n<p>Memento-Datetime:  can be derived from the resource URL but might be more convenient?</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p><b>External Content:</b></p>\n\n<p>Location: means redirect</p>\n\n<p>**Content-Location (no location header):  means proxy</p>\n\n<p><b>Web ACLS:</b> </p>\n\n<p>Link: &lt;...&gt;; rel=\"acl\"</p>\n\n<p><b>TimeMaps:</b></p>\n\n<p>None</p>\n\n<p><b>&lt;resource path&gt;.external - contains contents if binaries are exported. Otherwise, the file should not be present.  Empty file indicates 0 length binary resource.</b></p>\n\n<p><b>&lt;resource path&gt;.headers - contains headers</b></p>",
